   "q": "<div class=\"box\"><p><b>Grandma Hatice’s Tarhana</b></p><p>Grandma Hatice makes tarhana every August. First, tomatoes, peppers and onions are chopped and boiled until they are soft. Then they are mixed with yoghurt, flour and mint, and a dough is made. The dough is covered and left for a week, and Grandma mixes it every day. After that, small pieces of it are dried in the sun. Finally, the dry pieces are rubbed into a powder and kept in cloth bags. In winter, she cooks delicious tarhana soup with this powder.</p></div>\n<p>According to the text, which of the following is <b>CORRECT</b>?</p>",
